{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "ov5647",
  "vendor": "OmniVision",
  "part_number": "OV5647",
  "description": "1/4-inch 5 Mpixel CMOS sensor, 2592x1944, 10-bit, MIPI CSI-2. The sensor on the Raspberry Pi Camera Module v1, and this project's reference camera. Its modes are the ones this bench has run and read back; the full-resolution mode joins when a bench states it.",

  "provenance": {
    "derived_from": [
      {
        "kind": "datasheet",
        "reference": "OmniVision OV5647 Datasheet",
        "notes": "Structural facts: array geometry, native CFA order, chip identity, the 20-bit coarse exposure register, the BLC target pedestal."
      },
      {
        "kind": "measurement",
        "reference": "This project's bench: OV5647 module on Raspberry Pi 3B, values read back from the running part over V4L2 (2026-08-21).",
        "notes": "The gain law is bench-verified: code 200 measured as 12.5x, confirming gain = code/16, with the code range 16..1023 read from the control limits. The exposure clamp was confirmed live: maximum 1121 lines at a frame length of 1125, the stated margin of 4. Mode timing is the part's own defaults (line 2416, frame 1104 at 87.5 MHz); runtime blanking writes stretch these (this bench runs 2593x1125 for 30.00 fps), which is a control matter, not a mode fact. apply_delay_frames is stated from ecosystem behaviour and is promoted to bench-verified when the AE work exercises the write scheduler."
      },
      {
        "kind": "measurement",
        "reference": "This project's bench, 2026-10-14: the OV5647 read back over I2C (revela/sensors/readback.py) while it streamed each mode, 0x3000-0x5FFF.",
        "notes": "Which registers make a mode: those the datasheet documents as read-write in the PLL, timing, band-step, BLC and MIPI blocks, plus three undocumented analog/sensor-control registers (0x3612, 0x3618, 0x3709) that differ between the modes and hold still within one. Left out: exposure and gain (the AE loop's), registers the datasheet documents as read-only, registers that moved by themselves between reads seconds apart, aliases (blocks that repeat a base block in every dump), and undocumented ISP-area registers a static scene cannot classify. Line and frame length (0x380C-0x380F) are stated at the mode's defaults -- width plus default horizontal blanking, height plus default vertical blanking -- since at run time they are the frame-length control's. Both modes read out GBRG under the flip and mirror settings recorded in 0x3820/0x3821."
      }
    ],
    "gpl_driver_transcribed": false,
    "notes": "The Linux kernel driver drivers/media/i2c/ov5647.c is GPL-2.0. Its register tables are NOT transcribed here and must not be: that licence is incompatible with this project's. It may be consulted as a cross-reference for behaviour, and cited, but values must come from the datasheet or be read back from the running part, as above."
  },

